      "message": "This fails because tycho somehow doesn\u0027t find the egit source feature when building the p2 repository:\n```\n11:50:05  09:50:05 [ERROR] Cannot resolve project dependencies:\n11:50:05  09:50:05 [ERROR]   Software being installed: org.eclipse.egit.repository raw:8.0.0.\u0027SNAPSHOT\u0027/format(n[.n\u003d0;[.n\u003d0;[-S]]]):8.0.0-SNAPSHOT\n11:50:05  09:50:05 [ERROR]   Missing requirement: org.eclipse.egit.repository raw:8.0.0.\u0027SNAPSHOT\u0027/format(n[.n\u003d0;[.n\u003d0;[-S]]]):8.0.0-SNAPSHOT requires \u0027org.eclipse.equinox.p2.iu; org.eclipse.egit.source.feature.group 0.0.0\u0027 but it could not be found\n```\nI have no idea why.\n\nAnyway, this switch in the middle of the 7.9.0 period means that people in JGit will have to work explicitly on the stable-7.9 branch if they want their changes in the December release. EGit could switch much closer to the 7.9.0 release date; but the Oomph setup would be broken until then. Users have to check out JGit\u0027s stable-7.9 to work currently with EGit master if they have both in the workspace (like the Oomph setup does).",
